(A top-level buffer is one variable, held in one place, whichever way it is
 declared. Here it is declared with no value, and a function grows it by
 its name: the top level reads the grown buffer afterwards.)
To 'fill'.
    For each number from 1 to 3000, append "abcdefgh" to hold.

Create a buffer called hold.
append "a" to hold.
'fill'.
Print "after fill: {hold's size}".
